                  PSh_\infty(Orb_G)
                  \\,.
          %p
          #AssumptionsAndRefinementsInTheLiterature.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              (
              %strong> survey of available proofs.
              )
            %p
              Elmendorf’s theorem is stated in
              %a{:href => "#Elmendorf83"} Elmendorf 83
              as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              of
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer-Kan 84, Sec. 1.2, 1.7 &amp; Thm. 3.1
              to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"} simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presenting
              (in hindsight) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
              stated above (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Blumberg17"} Blumberg 17. Thm. 1.3.8
            %p
              Moreover, while
              %a{:href => "#Elmendorf83"} Elmendorf 83
              assumes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer-Kan 84
              allow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be
              %em any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
              to identify the fixed-locus-wise weak homotopy equivalences, used in the theorem, with the
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %p
              Later
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"} Piacenza 91, Sec 6
              and
              %a{:href => "#May96"} May 96, Sec. V.3
              re-prove the equivalence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              any
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              %a{:href => "#CordierPorter96"} Cordier-Porter 96, Thm. 3.11
              and
              %a{:href => "#Guillou06"} Guillou 06, Prop. 3.15
              re-prove a (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"}> simplicial
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              assuming
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
              or even
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Stephan13"} Stephan 13, Cor. 3.20
              %a{:href => "#GuillouMayRubin13"} Guillou-May-Rubin 13, Thm. 1.8
              re-prove the Quillen equivalence for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              again any topological group.
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Stephan13"} Stephan 13
              credits
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"} Piacenza 91
              with proving a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"} Piacenza 91, Thm. 6.3
              actually states, the conclusion follows with hindsight.)
            %p
              These results are all based on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              is proven in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#GuillouMayRubin13"} Guillou-May-Rubin 13, Thm. 5.6
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
          %p
          #AsAStatementAboutEquivariantConcordance.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (as a statement about
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+maps"} equivariant maps
              %br/
              One way to understand Elmendorf’s theorem (in its full
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
              of
