            this yields the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine+model+structure+on+topological+G-spaces"} fine model structure on topological G-spaces
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Orb
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb_G
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Orb
                        %mi G
                        %mi op
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}^{Orb_G^{op}})_{proj}
            for the projective global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
            from the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              There is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Φ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Θ
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Orb
                          %mi G
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Theta, \Phi)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    G\mathcal{C}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Theta}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{\Phi}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{C}^{Orb_G^{op}}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi X \colon G/H \mapsto X^H
              assigns fixed-point objects and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta S
              has as underlying object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(G/1)
            %p
              This constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the above model structures
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi fine
                    %munder
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Quillen
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi proj
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Orb
                          %mi G
                          %mi op
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Theta, \Phi)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    G\mathcal{C}_{fine}
                    \\underset{Quillen}{\simeq}
                    \\mathcal{C}^{Orb_G^{op}}_{proj}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Guillou06"}> Guillou 06, prop. 3.15
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Stephan13"} Stephan 13, Theorem 3.17
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Elmendorf’s theorem may be generalized to the case where only a sub-family
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
                of the closed subgroups of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is considered (
                %a{:href => "#Stephan10"}> Stephan 10
                , also
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#May96"} May 96
            %li
              %p
                There is an evident generalization of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
                of a fixed group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14
                ).
            %li
              %p
                The orbit category for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                can also be generalized to the orbit category generated by any small category,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                = succeed "-orbits" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                = succeed "-diagrams" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                whose strict colimit is equal to a point. If the orbits are either small or complete, then the
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                %a{:href => "Parametrized+Higher+Category+Theory+and+Higher+Algebra#PHCTIntro"} PHCTIntro
                and
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Chorny13"} Chorny13
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-CW+approximation"} G-CW approximation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tom+Dieck+splitting"} tom Dieck splitting
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bredon+cohomology"} Bredon cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} equivariant rational homotopy theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+equivariant+connective+dgc-algebras"} model structure on equivariant connective dgc-algebras
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+equivariant+simplicial+sets+and+equivariant+connective+dgc-algebras"} Quillen adjunction between equivariant simplicial sets and equivariant connective dgc-algebras
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic equivariant rational homotopy theory
          %h2#References References
          %p Lecture notes on Elmendorf’s theorem:
          %ul
            %li#Blumberg17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              , Section 1.3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/a.debray/lecture_notes/m392c_EHT_notes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/adebray/equivariant_homotopy_theory"} GitHub
          %p
            The “fine” homotopical structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spaces"} G-spaces
            (with fixed-point-wise weak equivalences) is originally due to
          %ul
            %li#Bredon67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Equivariant+cohomology+theories"} Equivariant cohomology theories
          %p
            The equivalence of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            to that of presheaves over the orbit category is then due to:
          %ul
            %li#Elmendorf83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Elmendorf"}> Anthony Elmendorf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Systems of fixed point sets
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1999356"} jstor:1999356
          %p
            Enhancement of Elmendorf’s equivalence of homotopy categories to an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+adjunction"} enriched adjunction
            and/or to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            based on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            and/or the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKan84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Singular functors and realization functors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/1385-7258(84)90016-7"} doi:10.1016/1385-7258(84)90016-7
            %li#CordierPorter96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"}> Jean-Marc Cordier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timothy+Porter"} Timothy Porter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Aspects of Equivariant Homotopy
                %strong 4
                (1996) 195 - 212 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00122252"}> doi:10.1007/BF00122252
                ) (Proceedings of the European Colloquium of Category Theory, 1994)
            %li#Guillou06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Guillou"}> Bert Guillou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A short note on models for equivariant homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~bertg/EquivModels.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GuillouEquivariantHomotopy.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Stephan10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Stephan"}> Marc Stephan
                ,
              %p
                %em> Elmendorf’s Theorem via Model Categories
                , 2010 (
                %a{:href => "http://web.math.ku.dk/~jg/students/stephan.msproject.2010.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                %em> Elmendorf’s Theorem for Cofibrantly Generated Model Categories
                , MS thesis, Zürich 2010 (
                %a{:href => "http://web.math.ku.dk/~jg/students/stephan.msthesis.2010.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Stephan13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Stephan"}> Marc Stephan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On equivariant homotopy theory for model categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.0856"} arXiv:1308.0856
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2016.v18.n2.a10"} doi:10.4310/HHA.2016.v18.n2.a10
            %li#GuillouMayRubin13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Guillou"}> Bertrand Guillou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rubin"} Jonathan Rubin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Enriched model categories in equivariant contexts
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1307.4488"} arXiv:1307.4488
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2019.v21.n1.a10"} doi:10.4310/HHA.2019.v21.n1.a10
          %p
            Other discussions generalizing
            %a{:href => "#Elmendorf83"} Elmendorf 83
            (i.e. the equivalence of homotopy categories) to general topological equivariance groups:
          %ul
            %li#Piacenza91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Piacenza"}> Robert Piacenza
                , Section 6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy theory of diagrams and CW-complexes over a category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1991-046-3"} doi:10.4153/CJM-1991-046-3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Piazenza91.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#May96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                et al., Section V.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant homotopy and cohomology theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/cbms-91"} ISBN:978-0-8218-0319-6
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/alaska.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MayEtAlEquivariant96.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            More on the approach of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer-Kan 84
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emmanuel+Dror+Farjoun"}> Emmanuel Dror Farjoun
                , Prop. 1.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy Theories for Diagrams of Spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2046572"} jstor:2046572
            %li#Chorny13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"}> Boris Chorny
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy theory of relative simplicial presheaves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.2932"} arXiv:1310.2932
          %p
            These Elmendorf-theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            (as in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Stephan13"} Stephan 13
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rubin"}> Jonathan Rubin
              ,
              %em Elmendorf constructions for G-categories and G-posets
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.08876"}> arXiv:2006.08876
              )
          %p
            See also related discussion of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbispaces"}> orbispaces
            ”, starting with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              %em Homotopy Theory of Orbispaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701916"}> arXiv:math/0701916
              ),
          %p
            relating to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#Rezk14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+Homotopy+Theory+and+Cohesion"} Global Homotopy Theory and Cohesion
              (2014)
          %p
            and then to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
          %ul
            %li#SatiSchreiber20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} Proper Orbifold Cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01101"}> arXiv:2008.01101
              )
          %p
            An n-cat café discussion initiated by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
            and probing some of its uses in Mathematical Physics, can be found
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2018/06/elmendorfs_theorem.html#more"} here
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+homotopy+and+super+M-branes"} Real ADE-equivariant (co)homotopy and Super M-branes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.05987"} arXiv:1805.05987
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03442-3"} doi:10.1007/s00220-019-03442-3
          %p
            Some generalization to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
          %ul
            %li
              Mehmet Akif Erdal,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of monoid actions via group actions and an Elmendorf style theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.06785"} arXiv 1609.06785
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s13348-022-00388-z"} doi:10.1007/s13348-022-00388-z
        .revisedby
